---
import ViewFrame from "./ViewFrame.astro";
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import { github, site } from "../site.config";
import aiSheet from "../assets/app/edit-with-ai.webp";
const ai = site.aiConnect;
const covers = ["starting-soon", "main", "live", "brb"];
const skill = `${github}/blob/main/apps/server/library-kit/skills/viewswitcher-scenes/SKILL.md`;
---
<section class="section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
      <p class="lede">Set up your views once. Then every show is a click away, and OBS keeps streaming the way it always does.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        {ai ? (
          <div class="vis ask on-dark">
            <Picture src={aiSheet} alt="ViewSwitcher's Edit with AI sheet, with Add to Claude Desktop and Add to Cursor buttons." widths={[320, 480, 640]} sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 11rem, 45vw" formats={["webp"]} loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="sheet" />
            <div class="made" aria-hidden="true">
              <p class="bubble">Make me a halftime screen</p>
              <ViewFrame show="fullcount" file="brb" alt="" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 11rem, 45vw" widths={[240, 360, 480]} />
            </div>
          </div>
        ) : (
        <div class="vis code" aria-hidden="true"><pre><code><span class="t">&lt;div</span> <span class="a">class</span>=<span class="s">"card"</span><span class="t">&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;small&gt;</span>Saltwater Kitchen · Ep. 31<span class="t">&lt;/small&gt;</span>
  <span class="t">&lt;strong&gt;</span>Sunday bread, start to finish<span class="t">&lt;/strong&gt;</span>
<span class="t">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
<span class="t">&lt;div</span> <span class="a">data-slot</span>=<span class="s">"Camera"</span><span class="t">&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</span>
<span class="t">&lt;p</span> <span class="a">class</span>=<span class="s">"caption"</span><span class="t">&gt;</span>Ana, at the stove<span class="t">&lt;/p&gt;</span></code></pre></div>
        )}
        <h3><span class="n">1</span>Pick or make your views</h3>
        {ai
          ? <p>Each view is just a web page (HTML). Start from the templates that come with ViewSwitcher or <a href="/templates">download free ones</a>. Or connect your favorite AI (Claude, Cursor or any app that supports MCP) in one click, and ask it for custom overlays and slides: "make me a halftime screen", "turn this sermon outline into slides". The <a href={skill}>ViewSwitcher skill</a> teaches it how.</p>
          : <p>Each view is just a web page (HTML). Start from the templates that come with ViewSwitcher or <a href="/templates">download free ones</a>, code your own, or have an AI assistant code one: the <a href={skill}>ViewSwitcher skill</a> teaches it how.</p>}
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="vis tiles on-dark" aria-hidden="true">
          {covers.map((file, i) => (
            <div class:list={["tile", { live: i === 1 }]}>
              <ViewFrame show="kitchen" file={file} alt="" sizes="10rem" widths={[240, 360]} />
              {i === 1 && <span class="badge"><i class="dot"></i>On air</span>}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <h3><span class="n">2</span>Click to switch</h3>
        <p>Click a view in the Mac app, or tap it on a phone or iPad beside you: pair one over Wi-Fi with a QR code, or plug an iPad in.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="vis"><ViewFrame show="kitchen" file="main" alt="Saltwater Kitchen on air: the dough up close, the cook in a polaroid beside it, and today's recipe card" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 22rem, calc(100vw - 2.5rem)" /></div>
        <h3><span class="n">3</span>Everything moves into place</h3>
        <p>Your camera, screen share and titles land where the view puts them, and OBS keeps streaming as usual. Nothing to rebuild for each layout. <a href="/setup">How to set up OBS with ViewSwitcher</a></p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 3rem 2rem; }
  @media (min-width: 60rem) { .steps { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .steps li { display: grid; gap: 0.85rem; align-content: start; }
  .steps p { color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 30rem; }
  h3 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
  .n { font: 700 0.9375rem/1 var(--display); color: var(--ink-3); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .vis { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; }
  .vis > :global(.frame) { height: 100%; aspect-ratio: auto; border-radius: 14px; }
  .code { background: var(--raised); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 1rem 1.1rem; display: grid; align-content: center; }
  .code pre { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(0.6875rem, 1.1vw, 0.75rem); line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink); white-space: pre; overflow: hidden; }
  .ask { background: var(--monitor); padding: 0.75rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: center; }
  .ask :global(.sheet) { width: 100%; height: 100%; max-height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 0 0; border-radius: 8px; display: block; }
  .ask :global(picture) { display: block; height: 100%; min-height: 0; }
  .made { display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; align-content: center; }
  .made :global(.frame) { border-radius: 6px; }
  .made .bubble { margin: 0; background: var(--monitor-2); color: var(--on-monitor); font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.3; padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 10px 10px 10px 3px; width: fit-content; }
  .code .t { color: #8a3b2a; }
  .code .a { color: #2b5c8a; }
  .code .s { color: #3d6b35; }
  .tiles { background: var(--monitor); padding: 1rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-content: center; }
  .tile { position: relative; }
  .tile :global(.frame) { border-radius: 6px; outline: 2px solid transparent; outline-offset: 2px; }
  .tile.live :global(.frame) { outline-color: var(--live); }
  .badge { position: absolute; left: 0.4rem; bottom: 0.4rem; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; background: var(--monitor); color: var(--on-monitor); font: 600 0.75rem/1 var(--text); padding: 0.3rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; }
  .dot { width: 0.45rem; height: 0.45rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--live); display: inline-block; }
</style>
